From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:25:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/28] feat(operator): serve the operator API on a listener of
 its own

DOOP_OPERATOR_DIRECT_ONLY tells a proxied request by X-Forwarded-For or
Forwarded, so it holds only behind a proxy that adds one. Traefik, Caddy and
Cloudflare do; a bare nginx proxy_pass adds neither, and its public requests
pass for direct calls (review of the direct-only patch).

DOOP_OPERATOR_LISTEN=[host:]port takes the API off PORT altogether and serves
it on a second listener (host defaults to 127.0.0.1), as Caddy keeps its admin
API on localhost:2019 and Envoy its admin port: a proxy in front of PORT cannot
reach it, whatever headers it sends, unless it is pointed at that address too.
PORT then answers 404 for /api/operator; the listener serves only the operator
API (404 for anything else) and needs no trust-proxy setting, so the audit log
shows the real peer. doopctl --url http://<that address>. Unset, nothing changes.

The direct-only note in .env.example and operator.ts now states its limit.

Tests (tests/operator.test.ts): with the listener set, PORT is 404 with the
token; the listener serves GET and a JSON POST, 401 without the token, 404 off
the API; [host:]port parsing (port only, IPv4, bracketed IPv6; bad values fail
at boot).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
